  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "2.3.1: Security - depends on patched System.Security.Cryptography.Pkcs (8.0.2 / 9.0.22 / 10.0.14) instead of the vulnerable 8.0.1 / 9.0.4 brought in by Microsoft.Data.SqlClient 6.0.2 (CVE-2026-84008 high, CVE-2026-70162 moderate). Packaging - built and published by CI from the release tag, so Source Link points at the released commit (the 2.3.0 package on nuget.org pointed at the 2.2.0 commit); Microsoft.SourceLink.GitHub 10.0.403 (build-time only). No API or behavior changes from 2.3.0. 2.3.0: Fixes - InsertModel works on tables with triggers (identity returned via OUTPUT ... INTO instead of a bare OUTPUT, which SQL Server rejects with error 334); composite keys: UpdateModel, GetModelByKey, DeleteByKey and Exists use every [Key] column (pass an object[] of key values) - a single value for a composite key is now rejected instead of matching on the first key column only, which could update or delete several rows. New - [RowVersion] optimistic concurrency (UpdateModel checks the version, throws DBConcurrencyException on conflict, writes the new version back; InsertModel writes it back too); [Computed] for database-filled columns (read, never written); [InsertOnly] for columns never updated (CreatedAt/CreatedBy); [Key(Order = n)] for composite key order; SelectMultiple/SelectMultipleInterpolated (+ async) for 2 or 3 result sets in one round trip; SqlServerHelperOptions.UseDateTime2 to send DateTime as datetime2 (default off, unchanged behavior). Packaging - 2.2.0's net8.0/net9.0 assemblies were stale builds without the 2.2.0 API; this package is built for all targets. Note: ISqlServerHelper and ISqlServerUnitOfWork gained members (source-breaking for custom implementers only). 2.2.0 (additive): interpolated read API - SelectInterpolated<T>/SelectInterpolated (DataTable)/SelectStreamInterpolatedAsync<T> (+ async), completing the FormattableString surface for queries. 2.1.0 (additive): transactions/unit-of-work (BeginTransaction/BeginTransactionAsync -> ISqlServerUnitOfWork); stored procedures (ExecuteProcedure/QueryProcedure/ExecuteProcedureScalar); ExecuteScalar<T>; InsertModel now writes back the generated [Identity] value; Count/Exists; attribute-resolved GetModelByKey/DeleteByKey; SelectPaged (OFFSET/FETCH); batch ExecuteInterpolated. Performance: per-column compiled coercion delegates, await using async disposal, explicit string/Guid/bool parameter typing, streamed bulk insert (no DataTable) + IEnumerable overload. Note: ISqlServerHelper gained members (source-breaking for custom implementers only).",
